    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyCaptureConfirm">Bind it</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyCaptureRetry">Press again</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyCaptureCancel">Cancel</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyConflictOwn">⚠ This combo is already bound to “{0}” ({1}). Two bindings would fight over it — change that one first.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyConflictOs">⚠ {0} may already be taken by another app: {1}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyApply">Apply</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyClear">Clear</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyInactive">No global hotkey is registered.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyAllActive">{0} hotkey(s) active.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyApplied">Registered {0} global hotkey(s).</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyApplyPartial">{0} hotkey(s) could not be registered — see below.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyFailedOne">{0} · {1}: {2}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyInvalid">Invalid hotkey for {0}: {1}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyCleared">All global hotkeys cleared.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.HotkeyNote">One row = one action + one key; one action can be bound to several keys. Modifiers are optional (F1 and Ctrl+Alt+S both work) — without one the key is taken system-wide. What lands on the clipboard: "capture region to clipboard" puts the **image** there, "capture region + scan" puts the **decoded text**. Wayland has no such capability — bind keys to the kscan CLI in niri instead.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Hotkey.Action.CaptureRegion">Capture region + scan (clipboard gets the result)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Hotkey.Action.CaptureRegionToClipboard">Capture region to clipboard (no scan)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Hotkey.Action.CaptureRegionAndPin">Capture and pin to screen</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Hotkey.Action.CaptureRegionWithAnnotation">Capture and annotate (copy when done)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Hotkey.Action.AnnotateClipboard">Annotate the clipboard image</x:String>
