    <x:String x:Key="Str.Hotkey.Action.SaveClipboardToFolder">Save clipboard content to folder</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Hotkey.Action.UndoLastAction">Undo last action (delete the file just saved)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Undo.None">Nothing to undo.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Undo.Done">Undone: deleted {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Undo.Missing">The file to undo is already gone: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Undo.Failed">Undo failed: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerToggle">Mark the cursor on the capture overlay</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerNote">Screenshots never include the cursor. Nothing is drawn on the overlay by default; press the toggle key to show the cursor itself (the capture then includes it too). Turn on the dashed frame below if you also want its position outlined.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerShowCursor">Show the cursor image as soon as the overlay opens</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerShowCursorNote">Off by default: nothing is drawn. Press the toggle key to show / hide the cursor; captures follow it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerFrame">Outline the cursor with a dashed frame</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerFrameNote">Off by default. When on, the frame hugs the cursor's real shape (transparent padding excluded), so it matches the actual cursor size; it stays visible when the cursor image is shown.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerColor">Frame color</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerThickness">Width</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerOpacity">Opacity</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CaptureCursorKey">Toggle key</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CursorMarkerKeyNote">Press the toggle key (Shift by default) to switch between "frame only" and "with cursor"; holding it down toggles once.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.ClipboardSaveFolder">Clipboard save folder</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.ClipboardSaveFolderNote">The "Save clipboard content to folder" hotkey writes the latest clipboard item to a file: image → PNG, text → TXT. Pick a folder with Browse…, or type the path directly.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.ClipboardSaveFolderPlaceholder">e.g. D:\Pictures\clipboard (empty = not set)</x:String>
