    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.Commands">Run commands</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandsNote">One JSON file per command under user/cmd/. A hotkey makes it global; saving re-registers hotkeys automatically.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandName">Name (shown in the list)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandHotkey">Hotkey (e.g. Ctrl+Alt+K; empty = none)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandRunAsAdmin">Run as administrator</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandAdminTag">admin</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandRunAsAdminNote">Each trigger asks for elevation: a UAC prompt on Windows, a Polkit prompt via pkexec on Linux. Without the box the command simply runs with normal rights.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandTest">Test run</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandTestAdmin">Test run as admin</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandTestStarted">Started (normal rights): {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandTestStartedAdmin">Started (administrator, elevation granted): {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandTestFailed">Test run failed: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Str.Settings.CommandEditHint">The dropdown lists "name (hotkey)" only; pick one to edit its program / arguments / working directory / hotkey below, then click "Save command". "Test run" starts it right away with the current elevation setting — no need to save first.</x:String>
